Fixed: a single-shot run (-p or piped stdin) used to exit 0 when the agent stopped mid-answer, and now it exits 1. This closes the last open row on #1016. Build, the full test suite, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass. The commit is c16eccb2; it isn't pushed yet, and the wrap-up push closes #1016 because the title says "Fixes".

What I found first. When the event stream closes before the run's AgentEnd, the loop just stops and treats the turn as finished. yoagent's finish() only logs that its agent task died, so nothing reached the exit code. The user got a cut-off reply with exit 0, the same as a complete answer, and nobody chooses that ending.

The fix. It checks what state the run was left in, not why it ended:
• `retry_safe_pipe.rs`: the gate now notes whether AgentEnd came through, whether output is piped or going to a terminal. If the stream closes without it, the gate reports the run as unfinished. This needed a one-line change at the loop in src/prompt.rs; that file's line count is unchanged.
• `interrupt.rs`: records a flag and prints (reply cut off: the agent stopped before finishing the turn) to stderr, or in the chat window in the REPL.
• `main.rs`: both single-shot paths now count this as a failed run. It exits 1, --output-format json reports is_error: true, and neither the watch command nor the opt-in auto-continue runs on the dead agent. main.rs wasn't in the task's file list, but without it the JSON output would have said is_error: false while the exit code was 1. I also rewrote a comment there that the change made false ("by here the run succeeded").
• Wider than the row asked, on purpose: yoagent sends AgentEnd on every ending it reaches normally (done, error, abort, rejected input). So the check also catches an agent that dies between messages, for example during a tool call, not just mid-answer.

What was and wasn't tested. The tests run the gate's real next() over a real channel. That is not end to end, and I found no way to make it so: a stub server that drops or errors mid-stream goes down yoagent's provider-error path. That is a different ending, and it already exits non-zero. Reaching this one needs yoagent's own task to die.

The tests that must stay unchanged pass with the filter on and off:
• a completed run, a retried-then-completed run, and a final-error run are not flagged when AgentEnd arrives;
• stdout is byte-identical.

I also checked that the new tests can fail: removing the AgentEnd record turned the "not flagged" test red, and removing the filter-off close record turned the cut-off test red. Both were restored, and no sabotage markers are left in the code.

